Enable gradient accumulation in simlingo_training/train.py
=========================================================

Why: with batch_size 4 on 2 GPUs the effective batch is 8, while SimLingo's
lr of 3e-5 was tuned at 48. Accumulation restores batch 48 at NO extra memory,
which is strictly better than either raising batch_size (needs memory you may
not have) or lowering the lr (changes the optimisation).

train.py currently builds the Trainer without it, so setting the key in
config.yaml alone does nothing.

--- a/simlingo_training/train.py
+++ b/simlingo_training/train.py
@@ Trainer(
         trainer = Trainer(
             accelerator="gpu",
             benchmark=True,
             callbacks=callbacks,
             devices=cfg.gpus,
             gradient_clip_val=0.3,
             logger=loggers,
             precision=cfg.precision,
             strategy=strategy,
             sync_batchnorm=True,
             max_epochs=cfg.max_epochs,
             overfit_batches=overfit,
             check_val_every_n_epoch=cfg.val_every_n_epochs,
+            # Effective batch = batch_size x gpus x accumulate_grad_batches.
+            # Defaults to 1 so existing configs are unaffected.
+            accumulate_grad_batches=getattr(cfg, "accumulate_grad_batches", 1),
         )

Then in config.yaml, at the TOP level (a sibling of `gpus`, not inside
data_module):

    accumulate_grad_batches: 6      # 4 x 2 GPUs x 6 = 48, == SimLingo

and restore the learning rate:

    model:
      lr: 3.0e-05

Check it took effect: Lightning logs the effective batch, and the number of
optimizer steps per epoch should drop by the accumulation factor.

Note gradient_clip_val=0.3 is hardcoded in train.py rather than read from the
config. Lightning applies clipping to the ACCUMULATED gradient, so this stays
correct under accumulation.
